From 59ddb3d0dbc9a9023d6e3ea6ad6dc538e4eaf74c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zed-patches <zed-patches@localhost>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 16:46:59 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_ui, editor: text in quotation marks is highlighted in
 the composer
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Zeo next proposal §6.40 (ask 64). A quotation sits inside a sentence, so
§6.12's row look would paint whole lines that hold other text. The quoted
text, marks included, gets a background of its own instead, through the
editor's text background highlights under a new key,
`HighlightKey::ComposerQuotation`. `HighlightKey::Editor` was not reused:
the editor's own navigation paints it, and clearing one would clear the
other. The colour is the theme's text accent at 20% opacity, as search
matches use a low-opacity accent, so it reads in light and dark themes
without reading as a search match.

It is recomputed at the end of `refresh_composer_blocks`, so the composer
and a sent message (§6.39, `set_source_message`) agree. Presentation only:
the text the agent receives does not change.

Pairs: "…", “…”, „…“, «…», ‹…›, 「…」, 『…』, and ‘…’ only when it opens
after whitespace or at a line start. The ASCII single quote is left out on
purpose: it is also the apostrophe (don't, d'água), and a scanner cannot
tell the two apart without guessing. The symmetric " opens only where an
opener can stand (not after a letter or digit, as in 6'2", nor before
whitespace) and closes only after a non-blank. A pair never spans a blank
line or a fenced block (the fenced rows come from `scan_composer_blocks`,
so the two scanners cannot disagree), marks inside an inline code span are
syntax, an unclosed mark highlights nothing, and a nested pair is covered
by its outer one, so ranges never overlap.

Tests in composer_quotations_tests.rs; Red seen with the refresh call
removed and `‘` opening anywhere (exactly the two GPUI tests and the
apostrophe test failed).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
